epic, pre-push validation will use the persisted structural oracle, exact-path guard, focused tests, scoped Ruff/format, comment hygiene, and diff check; the full-suite contract is delegated to Gerrit Verified CI rather than local make verify.","timestamp":1789052540488360001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution-plan correction: the original d6669496… oracle was stale against the reviewed parent 2697be85… because intervening mainline work changed protected prose in five paths and five allowlisted blocks in four paths. The 124 stable IDs still resolve one-for-one, and this leaf shortens every one relative to both old basis and current parent without touching the intervening prose. Rebased the immutable oracle to 2697be85… (14,024 target words), kept exactly 124 receipt blocks, and added derived docs/mcp-reference.md as path 19 after confirming no globally in-progress file-impact conflict. Per operator direction, removed local make verify from the leaf DD rows; Gerrit Verified supplies that gate. Initial focused run classified three documentation-contract failures (missing P1-P11 and stale generated reference); restored the contract and regenerated the reference. Evidence now: structural preflight PASS, generator check PASS, scoped Ruff/format PASS, comment hygiene PASS, diff check PASS, 42 targeted documentation-contract tests PASS; the broader focused selection previously passed 1,365 with 6 skipped before the final semantic wording refinements.","timestamp":1789056942609344001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Commit-gate correction: make lint detected docs/env-vars.md drift because condensing _config_resolvers.py moved a statically generated source-location citation from line 366 to 300. Regenerated the artifact (one documentation-only line-number update), added it as impact 20, added the generated-env-registry DD row, and extended exact-path and diff-integrity checks. No runtime material changed; no commit was created by the failed attempt.","timestamp":1789059165055230001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Committed the 20-path documentation-only change as 86eead289c546d98f2264986d7e4e17d086e050e (Change-Id I83c96f92d5d0f7610d693ed4338c805fc0a2e53f; DCO and canonical rebar-ticket trailer present). The commit hook passed lint and typecheck. All eight recorded post-commit DD rows passed: immutable-prose-only, exact-leaf-paths, generated-mcp-reference, generated-env-registry, focused-tests (1,365 passed, 6 skipped), scoped-ruff, comment-hygiene, and diff-integrity. No full local suite was run per operator direction; Gerrit Verified supplies that gate. Remaining before push: exactly 124 non-author semantic/bloat PASS receipt rows against this full SHA.","timestamp":1789059573927148001}],"created_at":1788570642317170222,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7d80448b-04f5-459c-93ad-decd82d844de","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"349e-8515-d8fc-48cf"},{"link_uuid":"ce0df70c-1482-4160-a507-90834a5e8ce8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"111b-008c-c326-4b19"},{"link_uuid":"887b27b9-388e-4793-bd1d-a9b0d4951ac9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a19c-02c3-2f52-4a6f"},{"link_uuid":"3d585a16-d393-4f6e-943f-3896f850992f","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"067f-d182-2c62-4dd2"},{"link_uuid":"ca51d9d3-fc1e-418e-aebb-afa6d2cd6dbb","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"88f4-9ecd-4874-4a0d"},{"link_uuid":"f3d8109b-6c4c-481c-bc5a-3e0c938863db","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"a6d8-cd8d-8e02-4491"},{"link_uuid":"d9eb8654-1c72-431d-8f73-942da006631d","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"26a4-936c-5c3e-4743"},{"link_uuid":"74efcb4f-fb0c-441e-ae37-3a163dc31273","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"77e8-b782-cd8b-462f"},{"link_uuid":"15b27928-b6ae-49a9-8e1d-96c249f89fe3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"c8d7-87ad-211e-44ac"},{"link_uuid":"e8d8d444-d2e9-4fb8-87e4-598ad45d0b2b","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1297-8b23-4b6b-4deb"},{"link_uuid":"5cb461b7-bdf3-46d3-9812-6b3ca9281f48","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5b3b-7537-d5f0-419a"},{"link_uuid":"94918502-5126-4440-b5c3-eb60141909a3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ed90-17c1-48bb-4863"},{"link_uuid":"19ecfca6-d09c-450a-8bf5-0d15992072f9","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"718a-c4b6-fcd2-49f5"},{"link_uuid":"5773ed14-10f2-4ace-8440-b62e4f3f5404","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"2450-21a0-1279-4a03"},{"link_uuid":"46e1eee7-5814-4077-ae21-29536f4d19f8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b7e6-dc75-342e-4965"},{"link_uuid":"7e66efa7-c576-4af5-a6e5-e2f1857376c8","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"94d3-fb3c-d3d6-42ce"},{"link_uuid":"4d0c9c4a-687e-4bc6-820b-71b89c615a29","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"cc01-7935-f8cf-4ddd"},{"link_uuid":"9f5417e3-de47-4220-b343-5b078e434c51","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1767-364e-ad82-4e93"}],"description":"## Immutable basis\n`2697be85ccc223c245815bc6ad818ebee2915c70`: 18 Python modules, 124 editable blocks (77 docstrings, 47 full-line comment regions), and 14,024 parent words (`\\\\b[\\\\w][\\\\w’'-]*\\\\b`). All stable IDs from `d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84` still resolve; intervening mainline prose is outside this leaf. Generated references are paths 19 and 20.\n\n## Boundary and stable allowlist\nOnly listed Python blocks and adjacent blanks may change. `D:<owner>` identifies a docstring; `C:<scope>:before:<anchor>` a full-line region; `:occN` disambiguates repeats. `docs/mcp-reference.md` and `docs/env-vars.md` change only via their generators and need no receipt rows. Full ID: `<path>#<ID>`.\n- `__init__.py` — `D:<module>; C:<module>:before:{import:rebar._config_coercion,import:rebar._errors,import:rebar._lib_writes,import:_store.push_state,logging.getLogger}`; exports, compatibility, push-state visibility, NullHandler.\n- `_alias.py` — `D:{<module>,_wordlist_path,_load,compute_genesis_alias}`; deterministic formats/persistence, fallback, warn-once.\n- `_child_env.py` — `D:{<module>,project_child_env}; C:<module>:before:_ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES`; secret-name registry and three environment projections.\n- `_config_resolvers.py` — `D:{<module>,resolve_fetch_timeout,repo_root_or_none,resolve_otlp_endpoint,resolve_detected_by,resolve_os_actor,snapshot_repo_root}; C:<module>:before:{_positive_int,repo_root_or_none,_gate_str_pref}`; resolver ownership, live reads, timeout/repo-root selection.\n- `_config_schema.py` — `C:CompactConfig:before:trigger; C:ReconcilerConfig:before:{dc_pandoc_timeout_s,max_acting_fraction,base_url}`; mirror omission, pandoc fallback, circuit breaker, always-on baseline.\n- `_config_sources.py` — `D:{<module>,llm_config_file_pointer,layer_llm_config_file}; C:<module>:before:import:rebar._config_resolvers`; pointer failures, deep layers, env names, retired aliases.\n- `_config_writer.py` — `D:<module>; C:write_jira_config:before:import:rebar`; sole writer, late root lookup, atomic write.\n- `_deprecations.py` — `D:{<module>,warn_deprecated_cfg_keys}; C:<module>:before:{<close-paren>,_TOMBSTONE_KINDS,_tomb}`; empty aliases, tombstones, warn/error signals.\n- `_ids.py` — `D:<module>`; authoring forms, four-hex warning, ambiguity, path safety.\n- `_lib_writes.py` — `D:{<module>,transition,claim,reopen}; C:claim:before:{import:rebar._commands,return:cast}`; exceptions, force shape, lifecycle semantics/cascades.\n- `_mcp_budget.py` — `D:{<module>,_wire_bytes}; C:<module>:before:{_LIST_TOKEN_BUDGET_BYTES,_LIST_REMEDIES}`; wire-byte budget/sizing and refusal over truncation.\n- `_mcp_errors.py` — `D:{<module>,js_safe_result,js_safe_dumps,install_js_safe_guard}; C:<module>:before:_JS_MAX_SAFE_INT`; error envelope, JS-safe range/conversion, registration order.\n- `_mcp_health.py` — `D:{<module>,InFlightGauge,offload_sync_tools,store_status,run_startup_store_sweep}; C:<module>:before:{_thread_offloaded,import:rebar._mcp_serving}; C:store_status:before:{expected,raise}`; thread-safe gauge, sync offload, readiness/instrumentation order.\n- `_mcp_inflight.py` — `D:{<module>,dedup_enabled,new_job_id,active_job_id,is_job_active,_register_standalone,begin_gate_job}; C:<module>:before:{_MAX_AGE_SECONDS,_STANDALONE_KEY_PREFIX}`; singleflight/private entries, age cleanup, leader/follower contract.\n- `_mcp_llm.py` — `D:{<module>,_structured_llm_failure,_with_attestation,_record_verify_completion,_review_plan_body,_spawn_gate_daemon,_start_gate_job,_register_gate_start_tools,_register_gate_start_tools.review_plan_start,_register_gate_start_tools.verify_completion_start,register_llm_tools.verify_completion,register_llm_tools.review_plan,register_llm_tools.sign_review}; C:_start_gate_job:before:if:handle-is_new; C:_register_gate_start_tools.review_plan_start:before:import:anyio.to_thread; C:register_llm_tools.verify_completion:before:ro; C:register_llm_tools.review_plan:before:ro`; tool shapes, polling/read failures, signer-context daemon.\n- `_mcp_models.py` — `D:{<module>,_OmitUnsetOut,PushStatusOut,WriteAckOut,FsckOut}; C:TicketStateOut:before:{cross_session_warning,author,created_at}; C:WriteAckOut:before:{description_warning,cross_session_warning}; C:CreateResultOut:before:duplicate_warning; C:GateResultOut:before:verdict: str; C:SignResultOut:before:ticket_id: str; C:VerifySignatureResultOut:before:trust_basis; C:PlanReviewStatusOut:before:ok: bool; C:VerifyCompletionStatusOut:before:ok: bool; C:GateRunOut:before:job_id: str; C:WorkflowRunOut:before:run_id: str; C:<module>:before:except:ImportError`; null/absence, JS safety, delivery/fsck fields, tool annotations.\n- `_mcp_opcert_health.py` — `D:{<module>,opcert_signing_status,run_startup_opcert_check}`; pinned-key comparison, serve-degraded posture.\n- `_mcp_reads.py` — `D:{<module>,_register_plan_review_tools.plan_review_status,_register_plan_review_tools.verify_completion_status,_register_plan_review_tools.gate_status,_register_bridge_projects_read,_register_bridge_projects_read.bridge_projects_list,_discovery_rows,register_read_tools.explain_criterion,register_read_tools.list_tickets,register_read_tools.audit_trail,register_read_tools.ready_tickets,register_read_tools.search,register_read_tools.verify_signature}`; status vocabularies, bounded lean/full contracts, guides/errors.\n\n## Protected material / consumers\nExcluded as concise/policy-load-bearing (15 blocks): `_mcp_budget.py#C:<module>:before:_DEFAULT_LIST_REMEDY`; `_mcp_health.py#C:offload_sync_tools:before:if:is_async`; `_mcp_inflight.py#D:{reset_registry,seed_stale_entry,_sweep_locked}`; `_mcp_models.py#C:TicketStateOut:before:inbound_deps; C:CreateResultOut:before:description_warning; C:GateResultOut:before:_omit_when_unset; C:SignResultOut:before:{envelope: str,signature}; C:VerifySignatureResultOut:before:rebar_version; C:GroundingBackendOut:before:name: str; C:GroundingInfoOut:before:dimensions_version: int`; `_mcp_reads.py#D:{register_read_tools.ticket_deps,register_read_tools.next_batch}`. Seven retired-pin alias regions are absent; replacements are listed/protected. Preserve the other 303 prose blocks, all inline comments/runtime strings/regexes/prompts/assertions/data, and executable AST. Keep 36 directive and 0 shebang lines exact with inline/next-code attachment. FastMCP exposes nested tool docstrings, and `docs/mcp-reference.md` derives their first-paragraph summaries. `tests/unit/test_plan_review_explain.py` requires all guide names in `register_read_tools.explain_criterion.__doc__`; schema/facade tests consume Pydantic/FastMCP tool contracts; the package docstring is public.\n\n## Independent receipt\nRequire exactly 124 non-author, leaf-linked TSV rows:\n`stable_id<TAB>full_before_SHA:path#ID<TAB>full_final_SHA:path#ID<TAB>contract_or_consumer<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>semantic_preservation<TAB>bloat_removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\nEach needs `after_words < before_words` and PASS in all three verdict columns. Missing/duplicate/extra/author-reviewed/short-SHA/non-PASS rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 124 allowlisted blocks shorten without losing listed contracts.\n- [ ] Parent/final parse with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`; attribute-free ASTs match after stripping only allowlisted docstrings and normalizing only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`.\n- [ ] Stable targets resolve; protected prose/directives/shebangs match; zero-context hunks stay within targets or adjacent blanks.\n- [ ] One commit changes exactly 20 impacts; focused tests, both generator sync checks, scoped Ruff, hygiene, and diff checks pass. Gerrit `Verified` supplies the full repository gate.\n- [ ] Exactly 124 fully cited non-author PASS rows exist.\n\n## Verification\nRun eight local DD rows: immutable-prose-only, exact-leaf-paths, generated-mcp-reference, generated-env-registry, focused-tests, scoped-ruff, comment-hygiene, and diff-integrity. Gerrit `Verified` supplies repository-gates.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/__init__.py","reason":"Condense 6 frozen prose blocks (382 base words); retain public exports, compatibility surface, push-state visibility, and NullHandler behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_alias.py","reason":"Condense 4 frozen prose blocks (338 base words); retain deterministic alias formats, persistence distinction, fallback, and warn-once behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_child_env.py","reason":"Condense 3 frozen prose blocks (588 base words); retain secret-name-only registry and the three environment-projection contracts."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_resolvers.py","reason":"Condense 10 frozen prose blocks (1047 base words); retain resolver ownership, live-read requirements, timeout posture, and repository-root selection."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Condense 4 frozen prose blocks (306 base words); retain current mirror omission, pandoc timeout/fallback, circuit-breaker meaning, and always-on baseline behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py","reason":"Condense 4 frozen prose blocks (483 base words); retain file-pointer failures, deep layering, canonical env names, and retired-alias shims."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_writer.py","reason":"Condense 2 frozen prose blocks (336 base words); retain sole-writer boundary, late composition-root lookup, and atomic write behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_deprecations.py","reason":"Condense 5 frozen prose blocks (1017 base words); retain empty active aliases, tombstones, and warn/error signaling."},{"path":"src/rebar/_ids.py","reason":"Condense 1 frozen prose block (358 base words); retain accepted authoring forms, deprecated four-hex warning, ambiguity handling, and path safety."},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"Condense 6 frozen prose blocks (775 base words); retain current exceptions, force shape, claim/transition/reopen semantics, and cascade behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_budget.py","reason":"Condense 4 frozen prose blocks (505 base words); retain actual byte budget, validated-wire sizing, and refusal-versus-truncation behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py","reason":"Condense 5 frozen prose blocks (756 base words); retain structured error envelope, JS-safe range, recursive conversion exclusions, and registration order."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_health.py","reason":"Condense 9 frozen prose blocks (1506 base words); retain thread-safe gauge, sync offload, store readiness, and instrumentation order."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py","reason":"Condense 9 frozen prose blocks (802 base words); retain singleflight key, private forced entries, age cleanup, and leader/follower contract."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"Condense 17 frozen prose blocks (2086 base words); retain tool shapes, polling/read-only failures, and signer-context daemon spawn."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"Co